    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Payments applied automatically, or across several references, are now spread in the new order, and `bin/e2e` passes both tests in the spec. I only changed comments after the run, not code.\n\nThe new order:\n1. **Overdue invoices first**, oldest due date first, lower id on the same date.\n2. **Then the rest**, largest amount due first, lower id on the same amount.\n\nEach invoice is paid off before the next one gets anything.\n\nThe change is in `recordAutoPayment` in `InvoiceService.java`. To decide whether an invoice is overdue, it reuses the app's existing status rule (`statusWhenPaid`) with the app's \"today\", so the week's grace after the due date still applies. Invoices paid in instalments, and retention (money held back) that has been released, count as overdue under the same rules used everywhere else.\n\nNo stored data or seed changes were needed. I also updated the comments describing the order in `payment-form.ts` and `InvoiceController.java`.",
